      "body": "<!-- proofline:finding-series=01a1fe5e-943c-7475-8f73-1c836a213921 -->\n**Warning** \u00b7 Concurrent console startups can abort during migration 002\n\nTwo consoles can read `user_version = 1` before either commits. The second then runs migration `002` using the stale version and tries to drop `legacy_format` again.\n\nSQLite rejects the second drop, so that console exits before dispatching its command.\n\nAcquire a write transaction before reading `user_version` and apply pending migrations without releasing that lock.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Details</summary>\n\nThe unlocked version read predates this change, but the failing drop on a version-1 database is new. Ensure the migration executor does not implicitly commit the transaction before running the SQL.\n\n</details>\n\n[View finding in Proofline](https://proofline.sh/orgs/by-id/01a1fe4f-49f1-7732-81cb-f1d6ad806605/reviews/01a1fe5d-1f35-7765-bfe1-edc3dbfb0630/findings/01a1fe5e-9440-7145-bb7f-1083221c2e57)\n\nAlso at:\n- [`console.py`](https://github.com/hasansyed-proofline/bench-proofline/blob/420baea889887b127f1c87d99f728e40f7664996/console.py#L29-L43) lines 29 to 43",
